                      (    forth6809.asm):06134         ; TSTCTRLFLOW - control-flow tests (glossary section 3.8, 22
                      (    forth6809.asm):06135         ; words - all except UNLOOP, which is a genuine runtime no-op
                      (    forth6809.asm):06136         ; and tested directly like ALIGN's own test, needing none of
                      (    forth6809.asm):06137         ; this section's compile-time harness). Every other test
                      (    forth6809.asm):06138         ; redirects CODEHERE to a scratch buffer (TSTCBUF), calls the
                      (    forth6809.asm):06139         ; real compile-time words directly (JSR IF, JSR THEN, JSR DO,
                      (    forth6809.asm):06140         ; etc - the actual routines the compiler itself calls, not a
                      (    forth6809.asm):06141         ; hand-simulated imitation), restores CODEHERE, then executes
                      (    forth6809.asm):06142         ; the compiled snippet directly. Tests the real interaction
                      (    forth6809.asm):06143         ; between compile-time correctness (right bytes, right patched
                      (    forth6809.asm):06144         ; offsets) and runtime correctness (right control flow) in one
                      (    forth6809.asm):06145         ; coherent check, without needing the outer interpreter, FIND,
                      (    forth6809.asm):06146         ; or a real dictionary entry.
                      (    forth6809.asm):06147         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):06148         ; Given the planned future application of the ANS test suite for
                      (    forth6809.asm):06149         ; broader standards-compliance coverage, these tests focus on
                      (    forth6809.asm):06150         ; this system's own compile/patch mechanism working correctly -
                      (    forth6809.asm):06151         ; not full end-to-end parsing, which the ANS suite will cover.
                      (    forth6809.asm):06152         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):06153         ; One case is deliberately NOT tested: DO with limit=index.
                      (    forth6809.asm):06154         ; Traced precisely (simulated the real DOTEST increment-and-
                      (    forth6809.asm):06155         ; compare-equal logic) and confirmed it takes a full 65536-
                      (    forth6809.asm):06156         ; iteration wraparound to naturally reconverge on equality, not
                      (    forth6809.asm):06157         ; one - true to the letter of "runs at least once" but
                      (    forth6809.asm):06158         ; impractical for a boot-time self-check. ?DO's own equivalent
                      (    forth6809.asm):06159         ; case IS tested (TSTQDOLPEQ) - its own skip check happens
                      (    forth6809.asm):06160         ; before the loop is entered at all, confirmed fast and safe by
                      (    forth6809.asm):06161         ; the same kind of trace.
                      (    forth6809.asm):06162         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
