                      (    forth6809.asm):07716         ; TSTDEFWORDS - defining-words tests (glossary section 3.9, 17
                      (    forth6809.asm):07717         ; words, 12 tests since VALUE/TO and IS/ACTION-OF are each
                      (    forth6809.asm):07718         ; combined into one test). Every defining word parses a name
                      (    forth6809.asm):07719         ; from the input source via WORD (HEADER's own mechanism,
                      (    forth6809.asm):07720         ; shared by :/CREATE) - a complexity nothing in section 3.8 had.
                      (    forth6809.asm):07721         ; Each test redirects CODEHERE, DPHERE, VARHERE, and
                      (    forth6809.asm):07722         ; SRCADDR/SRCLEN/TOIN together (a fake name, "TESTWD", reused
                      (    forth6809.asm):07723         ; safely across every test here since each redirect/restore
                      (    forth6809.asm):07724         ; cycle is fully isolated), calls the real defining word
                      (    forth6809.asm):07725         ; directly, saves the newly-defined word's own CFA (= CODEHERE
                      (    forth6809.asm):07726         ; at the moment the defining word was called), restores
                      (    forth6809.asm):07727         ; everything, then executes that CFA directly to verify runtime
                      (    forth6809.asm):07728         ; behavior.
                      (    forth6809.asm):07729         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):07730         ; A real, structurally important finding from this section:
                      (    forth6809.asm):07731         ; HEADER writes to the real LATEST variable unconditionally, not
                      (    forth6809.asm):07732         ; a redirectable copy like CODEHERE/DPHERE/VARHERE - every test
                      (    forth6809.asm):07733         ; here explicitly saves and restores it, confirmed necessary by
                      (    forth6809.asm):07734         ; reading HEADER's own code directly, not assumed safe by analogy
                      (    forth6809.asm):07735         ; with the other three pointers.
                      (    forth6809.asm):07736         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):07737         ; MARKER's own test is the one exception to the general
                      (    forth6809.asm):07738         ; redirect-then-restore-then-execute order: DOMARKER (confirmed
                      (    forth6809.asm):07739         ; by reading it directly) writes to the real DPHERE/CODEHERE/
                      (    forth6809.asm):07740         ; VARHERE/LATEST unconditionally too, so that test executes the
                      (    forth6809.asm):07741         ; marker word while still redirected, only restoring the real
                      (    forth6809.asm):07742         ; environment afterward - getting this order backwards would
                      (    forth6809.asm):07743         ; have corrupted the real dictionary pointers with scratch
                      (    forth6809.asm):07744         ; addresses.
                      (    forth6809.asm):07745         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):07746         ; Bare CREATE (never followed by DOES>) is deliberately not
                      (    forth6809.asm):07747         ; tested on its own - traced its placeholder "behavior field"
                      (    forth6809.asm):07748         ; (a genuine compiled JSR DOESRT0 instruction) and confirmed
                      (    forth6809.asm):07749         ; DODOES reads that field as raw data, not as code to execute -
                      (    forth6809.asm):07750         ; which only produces a valid jump target for the raw-address
                      (    forth6809.asm):07751         ; form every other defining word uses (VARIABLE, CONSTANT, etc,
                      (    forth6809.asm):07752         ; via CODECOMMA), not CREATE's own placeholder JSR instruction.
                      (    forth6809.asm):07753         ; Bare CREATE's own direct-execution behavior isn't meant to be
                      (    forth6809.asm):07754         ; relied upon before a DOES> patches it.
                      (    forth6809.asm):07755         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
C472 BDFC2B           (    forth6809.asm):07756         TSTDEFWORDS: JSR CRW
C475 8EC486           (    forth6809.asm):07757                    LDX   #TSTDEFMSG
C478 3610             (    forth6809.asm):07758                    PSHU  X
C47A CC0008           (    forth6809.asm):07759                    LDD   #8
C47D 3606             (    forth6809.asm):07760                    PSHU  D
